  "id": "partner-anchored-lateral-trunk-hold",
  "name": "Partner-Anchored Lateral Trunk Hold",
  "definition": "A unilateral isometric trunk family performed side-lying with the hips at the edge of a bench, the lower body supported and fixed by a partner, and the torso unsupported. The athlete holds a straight horizontal shoulder-to-hip line without arm support or trunk movement. Gravity tends to laterally flex the spine; that is a resisted tendency rather than a dynamic repetition. The hips remain fixed, so gluteus medius receives conservative mechanics-derived stability credit. Floor and suspension side bridges, lateral trunk lifts, Copenhagen holds, hip-abduction variants, and moving side-plank drills remain outside this narrow fixture.",
